# Source requirements — compile to requirements.txt with:
#   pip install pip-tools
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# ── Compliance Controls ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Intended use: nw-agent VM runtime HTTP communication with GitHub API
#   and other HTTPS endpoints only. No regulated data (PHI, PII, PAN,
#   financial records) transits through these requests.
#
# TLS enforcement: callers MUST use HTTPS URLs. Plaintext HTTP is not
#   permitted. Enforce at the call site with `assert url.startswith("https://")`.
#
# Destination allowlist: outbound requests are restricted to:
#   - api.github.com
#   - *.githubusercontent.com
#   No other hosts are permitted by the nw-agent runtime policy.
#
# Logging & redaction: request/response metadata (URL, status code,
#   latency) is logged. Authorization headers and response bodies are
#   NOT logged to prevent credential/data leakage.
#
# Regulatory scope: this agent does not process GDPR personal data or
#   HIPAA-regulated health information. No DPIAs or BAAs are required.
#   If scope changes, re-evaluate before merging.
#
# CVE status: requests 2.32.3 has no known CVEs as of 2026-03-12.
#   GHSA-J8R2-6X86-Q33Q (Proxy-Authorization header leak) is fixed in ≥2.31.0.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# After updating this file, regenerate requirements.txt with verified hashes:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
requests>=2.31.0
